/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_5/projects/spectral_collapse_ews/paper/sections/related_work.tex:13:\citet{martin2021implicit} applied Random Matrix Theory to weight matrices of pretrained networks, showing that heavy-tailed spectral density encodes implicit regularization.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_5/projects/spectral_collapse_ews/paper/sections/related_work.tex:14:\citet{roy2007effectiverank} defined effective rank as a continuous dimensionality measure based on singular value entropy, which has since become standard in representation analysis~\cite{rankme2023}.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_5/projects/spectral_collapse_ews/paper/sections/related_work.tex:15:In training dynamics, \citet{he2025spectral} linked spectral collapse of representation covariance matrices to catastrophic forgetting in continual learning.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_5/projects/spectral_collapse_ews/paper/sections/related_work.tex:16:Closest to our setting, \citet{gu2026sigma} proposed the SIGMA framework for spectral monitoring during recursive synthetic training, with validation on OPT-125M over short generation horizons.
